        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "claim_2c76e70d28184a25ad80db82593c874c",
      "statement": "LangSmith sandbox proxy rules inject a GitHub App installation token on the wire as opaque Authorization headers for api.github.com and github.com while the sandbox only sees a placeholder GH_TOKEN; proxy refresh preserves recorded repository and permission scope and a before-model middleware refreshes near-expiry tokens.",
      "evidence": [
        {
          "resource": "repo://openswe/sandboxes/providers/langsmith.py#L245-L265",
          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:2d0af139eed2b7e838e90fdafbffe930dd3f8de0867f03a5499d0f7cac7e907c:"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "claim_be58b0a576994be9b9832bbc8e629232",
      "statement": "The OAuth login/callback flow binds a random state nonce to the browser: /auth/login stores the nonce's HMAC in a signed state JWT and the raw nonce in a cookie, and /auth/callback verifies them with a constant-time compare before exchanging the code, resolving the login, enforcing the authorization gate, and issuing the session.",
      "evidence": [
        {
          "resource": "repo://openswe/dashboard/oauth.py#L325-L338",
          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:f87438a98790d6ae207d0721b6a262d630e2de77e11ea7277b8aa0b0f8503e07:"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "claim_2ef547e39e2e47b7b219fb10492c2671",
      "statement": "Post-login redirects are constrained by sanitize_redirect_to, which permits only same-origin relative paths or origins on the dashboard allowlist (DASHBOARD_BASE_URL plus DASHBOARD_ALLOWED_ORIGINS) and blocks known open-redirect paths, preventing a login link from being steered to an attacker origin.",
      "evidence": [
        {
          "resource": "repo://openswe/dashboard/oauth.py#L226-L254",
          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:33780048c2fcff32cc2548f44622f7c6c8cebb388e80d6d1dd827dac0aabd0e1:"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "claim_59a124937aed4d6a9e1b83504f22843b",
      "statement": "Cookie-authenticated dashboard mutations are CSRF-protected by an origin allowlist (require_same_origin / require_same_origin_for_mutations): safe methods are exempt and a request whose only credential is an explicit bearer GitHub token without a session cookie is exempt because a browser cannot forge it.",
      "evidence": [
        {
          "resource": "repo://openswe/dashboard/oauth.py#L605-L642",
          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:8021ceeb7fa8b1c075ed794fa5d0c56db925082d10f811ec7525bde394d8ad39:"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "claim_a0be89a0c4f34888a49c6b5eea00e6ad",
      "statement": "Desktop login uses PKCE so no session is placed on a loopback URL: the browser receives a short-lived handoff JWT carrying identity and the app's S256 challenge, and redeem_desktop_handoff mints the session only when presented the matching verifier via constant-time compare; cloud-terminal access uses a 60-second ticket bound to a specific thread_id and audience.",
      "evidence": [
        {
          "resource": "repo://openswe/dashboard/oauth.py#L476-L497",
